  "notes": "The HELLO/HELLO_ACK canonical trust point (register layouts HELLO_V1_LAYOUT / HELLO_ACK_V1_LAYOUT). The dual exchange is pinned byte for byte: Ed25519 signing is deterministic, so Go, the JCA and libsodium must reproduce every payload exactly; CryptoKit randomises signing and VERIFIES the committed bytes instead, round-tripping its own (the identity_binding precedent). The responder is deliberately the TRS-PROTO-018 hintless shape (zero EID). Negatives carry the mode a consumer must drive: parse_hello, verify_ack (against own_hello_hex), or ack_without_outstanding - the bare replay, which must fail with the nonce code BEFORE any cryptography runs (TRS-ENV-002).",
